WEBVTT

00:00:21.605 --> 00:00:23.065
Oh, my hair!

00:00:33.575 --> 00:00:34.910
Lot of weather we're having.

00:00:34.993 --> 00:00:36.328
Allow me, my lady.

00:00:39.081 --> 00:00:40.749
Shall we go a-trousering?

00:00:40.832 --> 00:00:44.336
Fry, I appreciate the gallantry,
but isn't this a bit much?

00:00:44.503 --> 00:00:47.089
You're right.
I'm sorry for showing my love.

00:00:48.298 --> 00:00:49.842
Okay. Fine.

00:00:50.008 --> 00:00:51.552
Here, take my hand.

00:01:05.107 --> 00:01:06.859
News and weather, everyone.

00:01:06.984 --> 00:01:11.154
I'm sure you've all noticed the bizarre
atmospheric conditions of late.

00:01:11.321 --> 00:01:12.865
Come to mention it, yes.

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:15.909
It seems something ain't right
in the magnetosphere,

00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:20.539
so I'm launching this high-altitude
weather balloon to gather more data.

00:01:24.835 --> 00:01:26.879
My pants! My lucky pants!

00:01:26.962 --> 00:01:28.630
They don't look so lucky to me.

00:01:28.714 --> 00:01:29.715
They are, too!

00:01:29.798 --> 00:01:32.134
I was wearing them that time
I found a dime in my ear.

00:01:32.217 --> 00:01:34.720
I was wearing them when
I won a subscription to Redbook.

00:01:34.803 --> 00:01:38.265
And I was wearing them when
I first met Leela, so yeah, they're lucky.

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:39.641
Aw!

00:01:39.725 --> 00:01:41.268
Also... Oh, Lord.

00:01:41.435 --> 00:01:42.561
Plus, they're my only pants.

00:01:42.811 --> 00:01:45.564
You've worn the same pants
for 1,000 years?

00:01:45.731 --> 00:01:47.316
No wonder they made a run for it.

00:01:47.399 --> 00:01:49.401
Whoo!

00:02:00.329 --> 00:02:03.832
Soon your trousers will slip
the surly bonds of Earth

00:02:03.916 --> 00:02:05.876
and ascend to the heavens.

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:07.419
I'm gonna blast that balloon!

00:02:08.045 --> 00:02:10.214
No way will I let God get my pants!

00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:13.634
Nobody messes with my pants!

00:02:14.009 --> 00:02:16.053
Not even the Holy One, blessed be He.

00:02:34.404 --> 00:02:36.532
Look out! A Central Park badger!

00:02:41.203 --> 00:02:42.538
I'll save you, pants!

00:02:42.621 --> 00:02:44.498
Scruffy, do you have any varmint grease?

00:02:44.623 --> 00:02:45.958
What viscosity you need?

00:02:56.343 --> 00:02:58.178
Whoa, there's writing in here!

00:03:00.055 --> 00:03:01.974
Also, this grease is flammable.

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:13.652
Incredible! Who could have done this,
the sewer mutants?

00:03:13.819 --> 00:03:15.612
No, this isn't mutant language.

00:03:15.821 --> 00:03:20.367
- We use a lot more profanity.
- Son of a...

00:03:21.743 --> 00:03:22.995
Leela, take my hand!

00:03:25.122 --> 00:03:26.164
I'm slipping!

00:03:26.248 --> 00:03:28.917
The one time your hands aren't sticky,
they're greasy!

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:32.254
Oh, sorry. Normally I would've
wiped them on my pants, but...

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:40.220
- Are you okay?
- I... Ow!

00:03:40.512 --> 00:03:42.389
My leg, it's broken.

00:03:43.098 --> 00:03:44.141
How'd you get down here?

00:03:44.224 --> 00:03:48.812
We made a rope from my shirt and jacket
and an expedition flag from my underpants.

00:03:48.896 --> 00:03:51.231
I'll help you up. Here, take my hand.

00:03:51.607 --> 00:03:53.233
Stop telling me to take your hand.

00:03:53.525 --> 00:03:56.361
Look, Fry, your noble gestures
keep making things worse.

00:03:56.695 --> 00:03:59.656
Can't you just be a rude,
unhelpful jerk like Bender?

00:03:59.948 --> 00:04:02.951
When I use up the toilet paper,
I don't put on a new roll.

00:04:03.368 --> 00:04:06.121
Fry, my friend, I found your pants.

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:08.749
And no sign of that crafty badger.

00:04:08.832 --> 00:04:11.001
All right! Lucky pants!

00:04:17.299 --> 00:04:20.385
Oh, my God! Look what my flashlight found!

00:04:22.513 --> 00:04:24.848
A huge pyramid
under New New York?

00:04:24.932 --> 00:04:26.558
What badger could've built this?

00:04:26.892 --> 00:04:29.686
And look at this intricately carved disk.

00:04:29.937 --> 00:04:31.939
It merits years of study.

00:04:32.022 --> 00:04:35.275
But how can we move
such a fragile, precious...

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:38.820
Ancient history coming through!

00:04:40.948 --> 00:04:42.324
No, no, no, no, no!

00:04:44.284 --> 00:04:45.536
Amazing!

00:04:45.619 --> 00:04:49.456
It appears to be some kind of
extremely ancient calendar,

00:04:49.623 --> 00:04:52.042
predating even the Girls of Sumeria.

00:04:52.918 --> 00:04:55.587
Of course. It's a Mayan calendar.

00:04:55.712 --> 00:04:58.966
No, wait. There's some dried-up
old stew on the screen.

00:04:59.383 --> 00:05:02.094
Sorry. I was eating a can of breakfast
and looking at porn.

00:05:03.971 --> 00:05:07.933
It's not Mayan, it's Martian!

00:05:08.183 --> 00:05:10.352
Amy, you grew up on Mars, right?

00:05:10.477 --> 00:05:12.229
- Can you read Martian?
- A little.

00:05:12.312 --> 00:05:15.315
I only learned enough
to yell at my nanny. Let's see.

00:05:17.651 --> 00:05:20.779
I think it means, "The sun will erupt,

00:05:21.363 --> 00:05:23.991
"all shall perish," blah-blah-blah.

00:05:24.074 --> 00:05:26.952
Get to the point!
What does it say about me, Bender?

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:30.247
Nothing!
But it does say a great cataclysm

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:33.000
will destroy the world in the year 3012!

00:05:33.166 --> 00:05:35.127
The world? That's where I live!

00:05:35.627 --> 00:05:37.171
Told you it'd say something about me.

00:05:37.546 --> 00:05:40.132
So the world will end in 3012.

00:05:40.507 --> 00:05:42.176
Why does that year sound so familiar?

00:05:42.301 --> 00:05:45.304
Because that's the year
that's this year! See?

00:05:53.687 --> 00:05:55.939
So, you all done with the computer?

00:06:03.363 --> 00:06:06.116
Is it just me, or is the world ending
more often these days?

00:06:06.533 --> 00:06:12.372
The calendar predicts fires, earthquakes,
sharksplosions, then it just ends!

00:06:13.415 --> 00:06:15.209
Exactly as the weather balloon foretold.

00:06:15.501 --> 00:06:18.003
Before Fry blew his pants out of the sky,

00:06:18.086 --> 00:06:22.049
it detected the onset of
a catastrophic sunspot cycle.

00:06:28.222 --> 00:06:32.059
It's starting.
This is the end of the world.

00:06:37.064 --> 00:06:39.525
Coward Man away!

00:06:43.111 --> 00:06:46.323
Some of us were crazy before it was cool.

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:53.247
Evacuating the planet in three, two...

00:06:53.497 --> 00:06:56.208
So long, Earth. Thanks for nothing.

00:06:58.710 --> 00:06:59.878
It's not starting.

00:07:01.171 --> 00:07:03.423
Come ons, comes on!

00:07:07.719 --> 00:07:10.430
Let me try, Headless Clone of Agnew.

00:07:12.891 --> 00:07:14.810
Damn thing just won't turn over.

00:07:14.893 --> 00:07:16.603
It's like Pat on a Sunday morning.

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:20.774
Oh, the Marconi is on the fritz, too!

00:07:20.941 --> 00:07:25.279
The electromagnetic storm is
disabling all electronics on Earth.

00:07:27.322 --> 00:07:28.657
Hi, there.

00:07:33.287 --> 00:07:35.455
Well, it wasn't a bad life.

00:07:35.664 --> 00:07:38.667
If only I could get back that time
I spent watching TRON: Legacy.

00:07:39.001 --> 00:07:40.460
Leela, I've made up my mind.

00:07:40.878 --> 00:07:45.799
Before we die, I'm gonna find and destroy
every remaining copy of TRON: Legacy.

00:07:46.091 --> 00:07:47.384
It may take a couple of hours, but...

00:07:47.467 --> 00:07:49.595
Fry, stop trying to do things for me.

00:07:50.012 --> 00:07:52.973
Whatever time we have left,
just live it with me.

00:07:54.433 --> 00:07:57.477
So, you want to join the Balcony Club?

00:07:58.312 --> 00:08:01.523
The Balcony Club?
I have an individual membership.

00:08:01.773 --> 00:08:05.194
- Zoidberg, get lost.
- I am lost. So long.

00:08:09.406 --> 00:08:13.243
Stop the end-of-the-world sex.
We might survive after all.

00:08:15.162 --> 00:08:19.082
All right, Amy, what's so important
that you interrupted my embalming?

00:08:19.249 --> 00:08:23.295
I translated more Martian symbols.
There's a way off this planet.

00:08:23.670 --> 00:08:26.381
That underground pyramid isn't a pyramid,

00:08:26.715 --> 00:08:28.133
it's a rocket ship!

00:08:29.551 --> 00:08:32.888
It was worth waiting five hours
to hear you finish that sentence.

00:08:33.305 --> 00:08:37.851
A spaceship made of stone?
With no electronics, it just might work!

00:08:38.185 --> 00:08:40.854
I'll stick with wind-up power,
thank you very much.

00:08:40.938 --> 00:08:43.774
Hmm. I've never flown a pyramid before,

00:08:43.857 --> 00:08:46.109
but I used to drive around town
in a mausoleum.

00:08:46.318 --> 00:08:48.028
How many people can this thing carry?

00:08:48.153 --> 00:08:52.282
Well, the mausoleum held
10 horny teenagers, so...

00:08:52.574 --> 00:08:53.617
Maybe 30,000.

00:08:53.867 --> 00:08:57.913
It's our moral duty to save
as many lives as possible.

00:09:00.832 --> 00:09:02.417
They had their chance. Let's go!

00:09:02.668 --> 00:09:04.711
Mind if I appear?

00:09:12.219 --> 00:09:13.428
Welcome to the Hidey House.

00:09:13.804 --> 00:09:16.765
Brannigan, tell me about this
freaky-deaky escape pyramid.

00:09:17.140 --> 00:09:20.519
I can fly it, sir.
I just need to know where, and how.

00:09:20.894 --> 00:09:22.729
The obvious destination is Mars.

00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:26.733
It's close, with lots of open space
and no Woodward or Bernstein.

00:09:26.817 --> 00:09:27.860
That's a plus.

00:09:27.943 --> 00:09:31.989
But we can only save 30,000 people.
How do we choose who goes?

00:09:32.239 --> 00:09:35.200
Well, let's see now. We'll need leaders,

00:09:36.869 --> 00:09:40.581
scientists, doctors, bureaucrats, pilots,

00:09:41.081 --> 00:09:43.959
valuable appliances, even janitors.

00:09:44.585 --> 00:09:46.128
But that's it. No one else.

00:09:47.421 --> 00:09:49.590
I'll miss you, Leela.

00:09:49.673 --> 00:09:52.050
But it's okay, 'cause then I'll die.

00:09:52.176 --> 00:09:53.719
Cut the waterworks, hippie!

00:09:53.844 --> 00:09:55.804
The final decision will be made not by me,

00:09:55.971 --> 00:09:58.640
but by a cold, logical machine.

00:10:00.225 --> 00:10:02.311
Who shall live and who shall die?

00:10:02.477 --> 00:10:05.606
Step right up to the
contrabulous choose-matron!

00:10:05.856 --> 00:10:07.858
I hate waiting in line to die.

00:10:08.108 --> 00:10:09.735
Move it along, grandma.

00:10:09.818 --> 00:10:12.279
Stick your hand in and take your chances.

00:10:12.696 --> 00:10:15.616
Female, crotchety.
Needed to keep others in their place.

00:10:15.824 --> 00:10:16.950
Accepted!

00:10:18.160 --> 00:10:19.203
Damn straight, kajigger!

00:10:19.286 --> 00:10:20.787
Ooh, me next!

00:10:21.413 --> 00:10:23.332
We just got one of these. Rejected!

00:10:26.418 --> 00:10:29.004
Male, scientist,
fond of crazy contraptions.

00:10:29.129 --> 00:10:30.464
Accepted!

00:10:33.217 --> 00:10:35.886
Female, scientist.
We were in the same sorority.

00:10:36.011 --> 00:10:37.429
Accepted!

00:10:38.180 --> 00:10:40.015
- Sigma Beta, see you later!
- Sigma Beta, see you later!

00:10:42.017 --> 00:10:44.686
Male, medical doctor,
delicious with butter and lemon.

00:10:45.020 --> 00:10:46.063
Accepted!

00:10:46.897 --> 00:10:47.981
I wish they'd hurry.

00:10:48.065 --> 00:10:50.067
I want to get out of here
before the mayhem starts.

00:10:50.234 --> 00:10:52.110
Mayhem? There's gonna be mayhem?

00:10:52.528 --> 00:10:53.737
I'm staying.

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:54.863
Hoo-ee!

00:10:55.489 --> 00:10:57.574
Well, might as well get it over with.

00:11:00.369 --> 00:11:02.746
Delivery boy, no discernible skills.

00:11:02.829 --> 00:11:03.997
Accepted!

00:11:04.581 --> 00:11:06.041
'Cause I like his pants.

00:11:06.250 --> 00:11:08.043
Yes! My lucky pants!

00:11:08.126 --> 00:11:10.462
Leela, we can go together after all.
Come on.

00:11:10.587 --> 00:11:12.172
Get your badge. Take my hand.

00:11:14.216 --> 00:11:17.719
Top gun pilot, natural leader,
extreme combat training.

00:11:17.845 --> 00:11:18.929
Rejected!

00:11:19.304 --> 00:11:20.514
What?

00:11:20.597 --> 00:11:23.642
With all spaceships inoperable,
we only need one spaceship pilot.

00:11:25.811 --> 00:11:27.437
Wonder what this doo-cracky does?

00:11:29.565 --> 00:11:32.192
Snake door. Roger.

00:11:32.526 --> 00:11:35.737
You can't reject Leela!
Give her a badge, you stupid box!

00:11:36.697 --> 00:11:39.157
Male, filthy hand, violent temper.

00:11:39.241 --> 00:11:40.325
Accepted again!

00:11:40.409 --> 00:11:41.660
No!

00:11:43.787 --> 00:11:46.832
Fry, the box has spoken. Go to Mars.

00:11:47.875 --> 00:11:49.001
Okay.

00:11:50.878 --> 00:11:52.754
Will you at least keep this photo?

00:11:54.381 --> 00:11:57.176
Remember how Bender dumped
all that pig's blood on me?

00:11:57.634 --> 00:12:00.053
You keep it. I'll remember you in here.

00:12:00.470 --> 00:12:03.599
I wish I could remember
with my boobs.

00:12:07.102 --> 00:12:09.104
Leela, we're off to Mars.

00:12:10.564 --> 00:12:12.107
We'll see ourselves out.

00:12:12.858 --> 00:12:15.277
Wait, I did it. I got Leela a ticket.

00:12:15.611 --> 00:12:17.321
How did you do that?

00:12:17.404 --> 00:12:22.409
Ah-ah-ah. A magician never reveals
his secrets. Except the Great Reveal-o.

00:12:22.492 --> 00:12:23.952
That guy stinks.

00:12:41.261 --> 00:12:43.722
I still don't see why
you get the window seat.

00:12:44.473 --> 00:12:47.976
Folks, this is your captain.
Our snake tanks are fully loaded,

00:12:48.060 --> 00:12:50.145
so once I figure out which
button launches this...

00:12:50.270 --> 00:12:52.523
I figured it out!

00:13:09.081 --> 00:13:10.707
Don't come back!

00:13:11.250 --> 00:13:13.210
Well, let's get looting!

00:13:14.336 --> 00:13:17.923
Fry, this is the most noble thing
anyone has ever done for me.

00:13:18.507 --> 00:13:19.883
Wait, Fry?

00:13:20.050 --> 00:13:22.302
I'm a lot of people, but I'm not Fry.

00:13:26.014 --> 00:13:27.182
Oh, no!

00:13:55.460 --> 00:13:56.920
Welcome to Mars!

00:13:57.004 --> 00:14:01.425
It is with heavy heart and open arms
that we receive Earth's only survivors.

00:14:01.592 --> 00:14:02.968
Admission, $20.

00:14:03.051 --> 00:14:04.845
Dad! Gleesh.

00:14:04.928 --> 00:14:06.180
Greetings, Mars men.

00:14:06.430 --> 00:14:08.974
We come to your planet
to construct a gleaming city,

00:14:09.266 --> 00:14:11.602
a second Earth on which to begin anew.

00:14:11.894 --> 00:14:14.188
Okay. Admission, $20.

00:14:14.438 --> 00:14:17.399
I can't believe it.
Fry sacrificed his spot for me,

00:14:17.482 --> 00:14:19.067
and I never even had
a chance to thank him.

00:14:20.027 --> 00:14:25.782
Don't worry, Leela. Earth is still there,
peaceful and serene as ever.

00:14:48.472 --> 00:14:50.057
Bender! You're stealing your own stuff!

00:14:50.307 --> 00:14:52.976
I am? Geez, I better slow down.

00:14:53.101 --> 00:14:54.978
I'm stealing stuff I don't even need.

00:14:55.437 --> 00:14:57.523
- You want a Torah?
- Nah, I'm not hungry.

00:14:57.814 --> 00:14:59.983
Aw, what's the matter? Scared of dying?

00:15:00.275 --> 00:15:04.821
No. 'Cause as long as Leela lives,
I'll be alive, too, in her heart.

00:15:05.531 --> 00:15:07.032
But really I'll be dead.

00:15:10.994 --> 00:15:15.207
Ladies and gentlemen,
our new Martian city is complete.

00:15:15.499 --> 00:15:18.126
I give you Dickfrancisco!

00:15:23.173 --> 00:15:25.759
The doves didn't magically
spring from my hand,

00:15:25.926 --> 00:15:29.096
but rather were crammed into
this netting sewn into my sleeve!

00:15:30.639 --> 00:15:32.140
Thank you, Great Reveal-o.

00:15:32.349 --> 00:15:35.769
And now, as a solemn testicle
to those left behind on Earth,

00:15:36.103 --> 00:15:39.773
I present this monument,
titled simply, "Heroes."

00:15:44.027 --> 00:15:47.656
That frightened little girl in
the statue reminds me of Fry.

00:15:49.157 --> 00:15:50.868
Stop the ceremony.

00:15:53.203 --> 00:15:55.455
Who is this non-Washington redskin?

00:15:55.747 --> 00:15:59.668
I am Singing Wind,
chief of the native Martian tribe.

00:15:59.918 --> 00:16:02.045
But I thought your people
abandoned this planet.

00:16:02.212 --> 00:16:05.090
We did. I just came back for my stuff.

00:16:05.382 --> 00:16:08.218
- What're you guys doing here?
- Fleeing Earth, of course.

00:16:08.302 --> 00:16:11.096
We flew here in your great stone pyramid.

00:16:11.388 --> 00:16:13.557
Seriously? That thing flies?

00:16:13.724 --> 00:16:16.643
Of course. Your people left it
so we could escape.

00:16:16.894 --> 00:16:19.521
I translated your warning
that the world was doomed.

00:16:19.730 --> 00:16:21.815
Not your world. Our world.

00:16:22.065 --> 00:16:25.027
We put calendar there
to warn you not to visit Mars.

00:16:25.235 --> 00:16:27.571
It Mars that gonna be destroyed.

00:16:28.947 --> 00:16:31.742
Why you think we so eager
to abandon this dump?

00:16:31.909 --> 00:16:36.205
You guys got 10, 15 minutes max.
Well, so long.

00:16:41.418 --> 00:16:44.087
Hey, Ancient Martian's
a very hard language.

00:16:44.171 --> 00:16:47.090
- A...
- looks just like a...

00:16:51.345 --> 00:16:53.972
- To the spaceship!
- There is no spaceship.

00:16:54.139 --> 00:16:56.600
You had it dismantled
to build that statue.

00:16:57.017 --> 00:16:58.477
To the statue.

00:17:01.772 --> 00:17:06.318
Oh, what an idiot I was.
And by "I", I mean "you."

00:17:06.568 --> 00:17:10.989
The final solar flare is going to
bypass Earth and strike Mars.

00:17:28.549 --> 00:17:32.886
My God, one of the hundreds of
contradictory prophecies is coming true.

00:17:33.178 --> 00:17:36.139
I should've known better than to
trust one of Fry's romantic gestures.

00:17:36.473 --> 00:17:38.517
Every time he says
he loves me, I get killed.

00:17:40.686 --> 00:17:43.397
It's just as I only now began to fear.

00:17:43.647 --> 00:17:46.984
The solar flares are igniting
subsurface gas pockets.

00:17:52.906 --> 00:17:55.284
Mars is being blasted out of its orbit.

00:17:55.367 --> 00:17:57.619
Fry, you noble idiot.

00:18:07.629 --> 00:18:09.965
You're right, Bender,
grave robbing is fun.

00:18:10.090 --> 00:18:12.384
And these piña skulladas are fantastic.

00:18:12.676 --> 00:18:15.554
The crazy weather cleared up, too,
for whatever reason.

00:18:15.762 --> 00:18:18.557
All in all, it's a fine day
for an apocalypse.

00:18:19.141 --> 00:18:21.268
So you don't miss what's-her-name?

00:18:21.393 --> 00:18:22.644
Of course I do.

00:18:22.728 --> 00:18:25.105
But even though we're
millions of miles apart,

00:18:25.397 --> 00:18:27.816
somehow, I feel she's near me.

00:18:27.900 --> 00:18:29.610
Very near!

00:18:35.115 --> 00:18:37.451
Oh no! The kajigger of Gibraltar!

00:18:48.962 --> 00:18:51.089
I have got to quit drinking.

00:18:52.758 --> 00:18:54.301
Thanks, friend!

00:18:57.262 --> 00:19:00.766
Another great thing was
she always had room for dessert.

00:19:02.976 --> 00:19:05.771
We're passing surprisingly close to Earth!

00:19:05.979 --> 00:19:08.607
When we reach 72nd Street, jump!

00:19:14.446 --> 00:19:16.031
Ah!

00:19:16.114 --> 00:19:17.157
Cushiony.

00:19:18.784 --> 00:19:20.869
We made it. We're back home.

00:19:20.953 --> 00:19:22.871
Okay, today is still a workday, so...

00:19:22.955 --> 00:19:24.081
Wait! Help!

00:19:24.581 --> 00:19:27.292
I'm still on Mars, and I can't jump!

00:19:27.709 --> 00:19:30.087
Hang on, Leela! I'll save you again!

00:19:31.004 --> 00:19:32.464
Or somebody else could do it!

00:19:38.262 --> 00:19:39.596
Quick, take my hand.

00:19:39.847 --> 00:19:43.016
I don't know.
Bad things happen when you say that.

00:19:49.898 --> 00:19:51.275
- I got her!
- Ow!

00:19:51.817 --> 00:19:52.860
Oops!

00:19:52.943 --> 00:19:55.654
- Try again!
- We're too far apart.

00:19:56.238 --> 00:19:58.991
No, we're not. Grab your
severed arm with your other arm.

00:19:59.324 --> 00:20:00.492
Ew...

00:20:00.576 --> 00:20:01.994
Okay.

00:20:02.661 --> 00:20:03.787
Hurray!

00:20:12.421 --> 00:20:14.840
Good thing Scruffy rescued Leela.

00:20:14.965 --> 00:20:16.925
Don't thank me, thank the ladder.

00:20:17.301 --> 00:20:20.637
Your cloned arms should be fully grown
in a month or so.

00:20:20.804 --> 00:20:25.934
But for right now, enjoy the sounds
of the world's smallest violin.

00:20:28.854 --> 00:20:32.774
I hope you're not too mad at me,
Leela, for tearing your arm off and all.

00:20:32.983 --> 00:20:36.028
I can't be mad.
I'm on way too many painkillers.

00:20:36.445 --> 00:20:40.240
Plus, you were willing
to sacrifice yourself so I could live.

00:20:40.699 --> 00:20:43.452
I mean, you failed, miserably,

00:20:43.911 --> 00:20:46.705
but you're the only person
who loves me enough to try.

00:20:47.748 --> 00:20:49.833
One last foolish gesture?

00:20:50.751 --> 00:20:51.793
Uh...